+- R-1066 — Low, `worktrees.restore_tree` CRASHES THE RUNNER WHEN A VETOED ATTEMPT REPLACED A FILE WITH A DIRECTORY: IT RAISES `IsADirectoryError`, WHICH THE FOLD DOES NOT CATCH, INSTEAD OF RESTORING THE FILE OR RAISING `WorktreeError`. Raised by the planner and reviewer of F027's first session at round 2's gate. SEARCHED BEFORE MINTING (checklist item 30): the open set is R-1065 alone, landed, and `restore_tree` beside `directory` in this record and its archive finds no finding. MEASURED at `cf6dc546` with a probe over a temporary git repository: a tree holding the file `a`, a worktree in which `a` was deleted and a directory `a` holding `a/b` was created, and `restore_tree` over that tree raises `IsADirectoryError: [Errno 21] Is a directory` from the write of `a`, because the sorted changed paths put `a` before `a/b` and nothing removes a directory standing where the tree holds a file. `_fold_task_vetoes` in `packages/orchestration/pingpong_job.py` catches only `WorktreeError`, so `run_job` raises out of its loop with the job's state last persisted as `running`. WHY LOW: a vetoed attempt must have turned a file into a directory, which no plan in this repository asks of a task. FIX: `restore_tree` removes a directory, or any other non-file, standing where the tree holds a file or a symbolic link before it writes the entry back, and turns every `OSError` of its own into a `WorktreeError`, so the fold blocks the job with `veto_restore_failed` rather than crash; a test pins the file-to-directory case restored and an unwritable path blocked. Owner: F027.
